province = 59
blurb = "Depicts travelers on a zig-zag path that disappears into a range of mountains on the right. To the left, a large Fuji towers over the landscape.

The figure on the left is a [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komus%C5%8D]komusō[/url] (\"emptiness monk\"). These were wandering Buddhist monks from the samurai class, usually rōnin (masterless samurai).

These monks wore straw basket hats called tengai to symbolize the absence of a self and to maintain anonymity. Due to the temperaments of the rōnin and the anonymity granted by their hats, the sect gained a reputation for harboring troublemakers and spies.

They played the shakuhachi bamboo flute as a form of meditation called suizen. A number of the pieces they composed and performed, called honkyoku, are still preserved and played.

The earliest komosō, predecessors of the komusō, are mentioned since around 1500, and were poor beggar monks without any social status in society. The sect was eventually abolished during the Meiji Restoration in the mid-19th century."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
